summary.text:
We need repair. The candidate latches outputs directly on individual button rising edges, regardless of step sequence. Functional failures show idle-cap-1: cappingConfirmButton true alone sets Packing_Machine true, but should not because prior capping machine not active? The public requirements say each step triggers after previous step completed. Need interpret likely outputs should sequence state machine, not independent latches. But execution contract supplement V12 says sequential process, step transition and output lifetime separate; when task says output continues working and names later start events without stop, retain until cycle reset. But does not authorize starting later outputs without prerequisite prior steps completion. The candidate allowed any confirm button to start its corresponding next output even without prior stage completion. Need add prerequisites: Filling_Valve should start on cleaningConfirmButton only if Pump_Motor active? Actually "After cleaning is completed, operator operates cleaningConfirmButton to trigger cleaning completion signal, automatically starting filling valve." So cleaningConfirmButton alone, if prior cleaning not completed/active, should not start filling. Need preserve sequence: each step becomes active only if previous step has been confirmed/done? More formal: bottleSensor detection triggers cleaning pump and continues. Then cleaningConfirmButton after cleaning completed starts filling valve. The fillingConfirmButton starts capping, but probably after filling completion. Thus if confirm pressed earlier before previous stage, should not start next. We need model stage completion flags/sequence with required previous active state.

Initial checkpoints idle-cap-1: cappingConfirmButton true, initial all outputs false. Observed Packing_Machine true because cappingConfirm edge set pack_latch. Expected likely Packing_Machine false because capping machine not running/nor previous capping stage active. Similarly idle-pack-1 packingConfirmButton true set Completion_Light; expected false because packaging machine not done? So prerequisites needed: cappingConfirmButton can only start packing after capping machine is active (or capping stage active); packingConfirmButton can only light after packing machine active; probably cleaningConfirmButton only starts filling after pump active; fillingConfirmButton only starts capping after filling valve active. Need maybe maintain stage flags. Bottle sensor can start cleaning pump directly no prerequisite.

But note outputs retain until finishedButton. A stage can be activated only once in cycle. Need prevent out-of-order edges from setting future latches. Current candidate triggers set latches unconditionally. We can wrap each set with condition that relevant prior output is TRUE. Example:
IF tmp_clean_edge AND pump_latch THEN fill_latch := TRUE; END_IF;
IF tmp_fill_edge AND fill_latch THEN cap_latch := TRUE; END_IF;
IF tmp_cap_edge AND cap_latch THEN pack_latch := TRUE; END_IF;
IF tmp_pack_edge AND pack_latch THEN light_latch := TRUE; END_IF;
Bottle sensor no pre. That would fix idle-cap-1 and idle-pack-1. Need check if cappingConfirmButton true while Capping_Machine true: cap_latch is true, so set pack. Good.

But maybe sequence cross: after cleaning complete, pump continues per requirement "triggers start cleaning pump and continues to work." So when cleaningConfirm pressed, pump remains true. fill_latch set with pump_latch true. Good.

Need ensure when fillingConfirmButton pressed, Filling_Valve is true (fill_latch true), so cap set. Good.

When cappingConfirmButton pressed, capping machine true, pack set. Good.

When packingConfirmButton pressed, packing machine true, light set. Good.

But note finishedButton resets all latches. After finished reset, pump false and future cappingConfirm doesn't set because cap_latch false. Good.

Need edit only necessary lines. Candidate output:
IF tmp_finished_edge THEN ... ELSE
    IF tmp_bottle_edge THEN pump_latch := TRUE; END_IF;
    IF tmp_clean_edge THEN fill_latch := TRUE; END_IF;
...
We can change four IFs. Need ensure comments contract maybe contradictory: says "Filling_Valve: activation=rising edge cleaningConfirmButton (PUB002); hold until finishedButton...)" but omits prerequisite. Could update comment maybe not necessary but nice. We need exact unique substrings. Use JSON edits. Could replace the four IF blocks with conditions.

Also maybe output contract comment says activation by edges only but not sequencing; update? The repair request says update contradictory comment when needed. We can include comment edit but not needed for functional. However if we retain comment saying activation=rising edge cleaningConfirmButton regardless sequence, it's contradictory. Could add "when prerequisite Pump_Motor is active". But edit comment might be larger. Need make minimal semantic fix. We can replace the block:
    IF tmp_clean_edge THEN
        fill_latch := TRUE;
    END_IF;

    IF tmp_fill_edge THEN
        cap_latch := TRUE;
    END_IF;

    IF tmp_cap_edge THEN
        pack_latch := TRUE;
    END_IF;

    IF tmp_pack_edge THEN
        light_latch := TRUE;
    END_IF;

with prerequisites. But note exact substring from candidate includes newlines. Need ensure old string exactly unique. We'll provide one edit.

Let's construct old:
    IF tmp_clean_edge THEN
        fill_latch := TRUE;
    END_IF;

    IF tmp_fill_edge THEN
        cap_latch := TRUE;
    END_IF;

    IF tmp_cap_edge THEN
        pack_latch := TRUE;
    END_IF;

    IF tmp_pack_edge THEN
        light_latch := TRUE;
    END_IF;

New:
    IF tmp_clean_edge AND pump_latch THEN
        fill_latch := TRUE;
    END_IF;

    IF tmp_fill_edge AND fill_latch THEN
        cap_latch := TRUE;
    END_IF;

    IF tmp_cap_edge AND cap_latch THEN
        pack_latch := TRUE;
    END_IF;

    IF tmp_pack_edge AND pack_latch THEN
        light_latch := TRUE;
    END_IF;

Need ensure pump_latch is updated earlier? In same scan if bottleSensor rising and cleaningConfirmButton rising simultaneously, pump_latch set before check? In code, pump set first in separate IF tmp_bottle_edge then later tmp_clean_edge checks pump_latch. Since sequential, if both edges true, pump_latch true, so fill_latch set. Good.

But potential issue: cleaningConfirmButton should start filling after cleaning completed. Pump active indicates cleaning process started, not necessarily completed? In requirements, "When sensor detects bottle, triggers start cleaning pump and continues to work. After cleaning completed, operator operates button cleaningConfirmButton..." How does system know cleaning completed? The operator button is confirmation; the pump may still be running until operator confirms? Actually cleaning pump continues to work indefinitely. The operator presses cleaningConfirmButton when cleaning is completed. There is no separate completion sensor. So prerequisite pump active is correct.

Need maybe if cleaningConfirmButton pressed before bottle sensor, pump false so no filling. Good.

What about bottleSensor repeats while cycle? It may remain true? R_TRIG only on rising. Good.

Also check idle cases with cappingConfirm true: pump_latch false, cap_latch false, so condition tmp_cap_edge AND cap_latch false, pack not set. Capping_Machine output false. Good.

One more subtlety: after capping machine active, cap_latch true. If cappingConfirmButton true again maybe irrelevant. Good.

No need reset individual stage flags except finished resets all.

Let's produce JSON edit.

